### ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Employee API — hire (POST /api/v1/stores/{storeId}/employees)
#
# How to run: VS Code REST Client — click "Send Request" top to bottom
# (captures feed the next requests; never re-type values by hand).
#
# Prerequisites:
#   - Docker stack rebuilt with the Employee module: docker compose up -d --build
#   - Seeded chain admin exists: admin@devtunde.com / Password123!
#   - Company email domain in the dev stack: devtunde.com
#
# `# Expected:` labels the status code each request proves.
# Re-running the file later is safe — {{$timestamp}} mints fresh personas.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000

### 1. Chain admin logs in
# @name adminLogin
# Expected: 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 2. Mint the store's seat admin (fresh persona per run)
# @name seatSignup
# Expected: 201 (409 on a same-second re-run — also fine)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Probe Seat Admin",
  "email": "emp-seat-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348091234567"
}

### 3. Seat admin logs in (the response carries their publicId)
# @name seatLogin
# Expected: 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{seatSignup.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 4. Chain admin creates the store, seating that admin
# @name store
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "brand": "Employee Hire Probe {{$timestamp}}",
  "storeType": "KIOSK",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{seatLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "Probe Way",
    "phone": "08012345678",
    "email": "emp-hire-store-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com"
  }
}

### 5. Seat admin hires a cashier — Door 1: unknown work email → new account
# @name hire
# Expected: 201 — and no password, no tokens anywhere in the body
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores/{{store.response.body.publicId}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{seatLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Probe Cashier",
  "email": "emp-cashier-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348091234567",
  "jobTitle": "CASHIER"
}

### 6. Chain admin also hires — the dual gate lets both authorities in
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores/{{store.response.body.publicId}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Probe Attendant",
  "email": "emp-attendant-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348091234567",
  "jobTitle": "SALES_ATTENDANT"
}

### 7. Door 2 — hiring the SAME actively-employed person again: 409
# Expected: 409 (employee-already-employed) — email chained from request 5
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores/{{store.response.body.publicId}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{seatLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Probe Cashier Again",
  "email": "{{hire.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348091234567",
  "jobTitle": "MANAGER"
}

### 8. Personal-domain email refused at the boundary
# Expected: 400 (invalid-work-email)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores/{{store.response.body.publicId}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{seatLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Shopper Person",
  "email": "probe.shopper@gmail.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348091234567",
  "jobTitle": "CASHIER"
}

### 9. Made-up job title refused
# Expected: 400 (the body cannot map "CEO" onto the title enum)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores/{{store.response.body.publicId}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{seatLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Probe CEO",
  "email": "emp-ceo-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348091234567",
  "jobTitle": "CEO"
}

### 10. Garbage phone refused (provisioning reuses signup's E.164 rules)
# Expected: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores/{{store.response.body.publicId}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{seatLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Probe Phone",
  "email": "emp-phone-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "not-a-phone",
  "jobTitle": "CASHIER"
}

### 11. Blank full name refused
# Expected: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores/{{store.response.body.publicId}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{seatLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "   ",
  "email": "emp-blank-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348091234567",
  "jobTitle": "CASHIER"
}

### 12. Unknown store: 404 — dead stores stay hidden
# Expected: 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Ghost Staff",
  "email": "emp-ghost-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348091234567",
  "jobTitle": "CASHIER"
}

### 13. Mint a regular user (no authority anywhere)
# @name nobody
# Expected: 201 (409 on a same-second re-run — also fine)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Nobody",
  "email": "emp-nobody-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348091234567"
}

### 14. Nobody logs in
# @name nobodyLogin
# Expected: 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{nobody.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 15. Regular user hire attempt bounces: 403
# Expected: 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores/{{store.response.body.publicId}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{nobodyLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Probe Snoop",
  "email": "emp-snoop-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348091234567",
  "jobTitle": "CASHIER"
}

### 16. No token at all: 401
# Expected: 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores/{{store.response.body.publicId}}/employees
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Tokenless",
  "email": "emp-tokenless-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348091234567",
  "jobTitle": "CASHIER"
}

### 17. Mixed-case work domain accepted (review fix: case-insensitive gate)
# Expected: 201 — and user.email comes back lower-cased (normalized at identity creation)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores/{{store.response.body.publicId}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{seatLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Chidi Mixed Case",
  "email": "emp-mixed-{{$timestamp}}@DevTunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348091234567",
  "jobTitle": "CASHIER"
}

